  "text": "<p><strong>Time allowed:</strong> 90 minutes. <strong>Total:</strong> 100 points across 18 questions.</p><p>This exam considers water and energy use on a fictional campus. All measurements, estimates, and scenarios are supplied for this exam; no outside information is required. Questions are independent.</p><p>A non-programmable calculator is permitted. Give units where requested and keep at least three significant figures during calculations. Show your reasoning where asked. Equivalent expressions and well-supported alternative explanations are accepted.</p><p>For choice questions, mark your selection clearly. For ordering questions, write sequence numbers in the boxes and leave unused alternatives blank. Write and draw in the spaces provided; label any additional work with its question number.</p>"
